    "done_when": "Frame 44 re-solved at the revision that wrote the stored artifact reproduces its stored residual 0.4499 to 3.3e-16, while today's code returns 0.2338 with the same driver, seed, coil currents, target, tolerance and options. The report /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/mulw-gate-frame-solver-evolution.md names the solver commit that moves frame 44, found by comparing named revisions (no git bisect, no stash, no checkout in the shared tree: extract each revision's nova/ with git archive into the run directory and run it there), attributes frames 144, 146, 137 and 179 to that or another named commit, and states, with the terminal residual per frame at today's head, whether these frames converge under the production route and if not what the measured obstruction is. Each re-solve runs as ONE H200 job (betelgeuse, reservation gpu_0003_grpA, one card, 8 CPUs, an explicit --mem, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python without uv, submitted with RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 sbatch, which is a separate job on the H200 node and not a step of the fleet allocation the HOST line describes, and is authorised; never srun or salloc. Submit for real and read squeue after a minute; only if it is still PENDING on a resource or configuration reason resubmit to titan (--partition=titan --gres=gpu:1) and say so; CPU in place on the fleet node is the last rung and its walls are not the GPU measurement, --mem=64G) holding all revisions and frames sequentially, each row persisted as it lands. The fragment docs/evidence/fragments/multi-unit-limiter-wall/mulw-gate-frame-solver-evolution.html tables frame by revision by residual and carries a line-contour panel of frame 44 at both revisions on shared levels with both null sets and the wall. No source under nova/ is edited. If the job outlasts your turn, commit, write status waiting with the sacct probe as wait_probe and the job id in wait_condition, and end the turn; the recovery sweep resumes you when the job is terminal. Keep scratch under the run directory, not /tmp, which is at 91 percent on the fleet node; a baseline arm extracts only the subtrees it imports and removes them before the manifest. This gate measures only this node; a failure outside its scope goes under follow_ons.",
